      "text": "$\\ds (a,b)^T$ is an eigenvector with eigenvalue $\\ds ab$.  Hence,\n\n[mathbb{P} = a \\begin{pmatrix} a \\\\ b \\end{pmatrix} + b \\begin{pmatrix} -a \\\\ -b \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} a^2 + b^2 & ab \\\\ -a b & a^2 + b^2 \\end{pmatrix} ]\n\nbecause it projects onto $\\begin{pmatrix} a \\\\ b \\end{pmatrix}$.  Therefore, if $\\mathbb{P}^{-1}$ exists, it will be the same matrix, but with these columns swapped.  Thus, $\\mathbb{P}^{-1} = \\pmatrix{ -3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3}$ and so $\\mathbb{P}^{-1} = -2 \\cdot \\mathbb{P}^T.$",
